      "message": "I was thinking: if you really need a debug dump, dumb CSRs is useful than others.\n\nE.g.:\nCSR_VIC_MICAUSE\nCSR_VIC_MIPEND_G0\n\nThis CL https://crrev.com/c/2167115/9/chip/mt8192_scp/intc.c is quite old, but some idea inside.\n\n\nOtherwise, we have some encoded data in TP (see https://crrev.com/c/2638998).  I guess you could encode the ec_int to make it obviously a group number.\n\nE.g.: you have 4 bytes to put ec_int (https://crrev.com/c/2638998/6/core/riscv-rv32i/init.S#349).  Makes the first bit to \"1\" or whatever magic number to indicate the following bits is a group number.",
